The registry-first sample tests/registry/is.jsonl contains addresses, postcodes and coordinates
from Staðfangaskrá, the access address register of Húsnæðis- og mannvirkjastofnun (HMS), read
from its WFS (public:Stadfangaskra) on 2026-10-30. Byggir á upplýsingum frá HMS
(https://hms.is/stadfangaskra). Used under the Icelandic guidelines on reuse of public
information (Leiðbeiningar varðandi endurnot opinberra upplýsinga), as the dataset's metadata
states.

Its post towns come from Póstnúmeraskrá, the postcode register of Byggðastofnun
(postnumeraskra_2024.xlsx, https://www.byggdastofnun.is/is/postthjonusta/postnumer). Byggt á
gögnum frá Byggðastofnun.

Its municipality names come from "IS 50V Mörk sveitarfélaga" (IS_50V:mork_sveitarf_flakar,
release of 2026-09-24) by Náttúrufræðistofnun, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution
4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Changes: the three files were joined by postcode and municipality number
(tests/registry/stadfangaskra-csv.sql, which reads IS 50V's municipality number 3506 as the
register's 3609 for Borgarbyggð) and a sample drawn; the query forms were constructed from the
fields, not by HMS, Byggðastofnun or Náttúrufræðistofnun, none of which has approved this sample.
Per-case file checksums and retrieval dates are recorded in the corpus;
docs/evaluation/registry/is.md records the upstream checksums.
